From d0bdcb4c978552c284b2e303bce3c2c1293936d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gregor.fuis" <gregor.fuis@fora.si>
Date: Sat, 6 Dec 2025 09:18:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat,avcodec: Add SCTE-35 support with stream-level CUEI
 handling

This patch adds comprehensive SCTE-35 (digital program insertion cueing)
support to FFmpeg, including proper handling of both program-level and
stream-level CUEI registration descriptors.

Changes include:

1. avcodec: Add AVTransportTimestamp side data type
   - New structure to preserve original PTS values from demuxer
   - Enables proper pts_adjustment calculation for SCTE-35 packets

2. mpegts demuxer: Stash original PTS for SCTE-35 sections
   - Store transport timestamp as side data for SCTE-35 streams
   - Use video stream PTS instead of PCR for more accurate timing
   - Add stream-level CUEI registration descriptor support

3. mpegtsenc muxer: Add SCTE-35 output support
   - Handle SCTE-35 as sections (not PES packets)
   - Add CUEI registration descriptor at program level
   - Add Cue Identifier Descriptor (0x8a) in stream descriptors
   - Auto-insert scte35ptsadjust bitstream filter

4. bsf: Add scte35ptsadjust bitstream filter
   - Adjusts pts_adjustment field in SCTE-35 packets
   - Compensates for timing changes during remuxing

5. mux: Exclude SCTE-35 from interleaved streams
   - Similar to SMPTE 2038 handling

Tested with streams containing both program-level and stream-level
CUEI registration descriptors. SCTE-35 sections correctly pass through
during remuxing and transcoding operations.
